            <ArticleTitle>Safety considerations when promoting exercise in individuals with serious mental illness.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>220-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.psychres.2009.11.017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Histories and physical exams, completed prior to starting a weight loss program, showed that 52% (N=106) had high risk for coronary artery disease (CAD), 40% had difficulty performing a tandem gait (indicator of balance), and 30% had an existing musculoskeletal disorder. These risks are realistic concerns when recommending exercise and/or walking.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
